  "term": "conduct disorder",
  "definition": "Conduct disorder is a diagnosis marked by an ongoing pattern of behavior in which a young person violates other people’s basic rights or major age-expected rules and social norms. It can involve aggression toward people or animals, damage to property, deceit or theft, and serious rule-breaking, with onset before age 18.",
